    "exit_rule": "drawer_position >= 0.29 at the final state (the demonstrated open stop is 0.30)",
    "guidance": "**Use:** Drawer-frame Cartesian prior requiring accurate `drawer_origin_world_m`, unit `drawer_orientation_wxyz` (local -X is opening), and `desired_open_position_m > 0.26` (trained at 0.300 m). Its documented purpose is following a reliably calibrated displaced drawer, but no displaced-drawer rollout was validated. In the nominal in-distribution test it passed only 3/12 runs (25%); the three passing final positions were 0.29976–0.30000 m. Therefore it is not the nominal default and no broadly reliable regime beyond those individual runs was established.\n\n**Avoid:** Prefer H03 for nominal geometry. Avoid H01 with uncertain/stale drawer calibration, large or unreachable displacement, missed/blocked front contact, or independently displaced/noisy red pose. Entry after nonzero opening and shifted cabinets are design intentions, not validated conditions.\n\n**Failure recognition:** Require the physical final/current drawer position, not a transient maximum. Six failed runs crossed 0.29 m and then ended at 0.16345–0.26554 m; three other failures never crossed 0.29 m. Treat regression, lack of progress, inconsistent TCP/front geometry, calibration jumps, red/TCP misalignment, closure without red co-motion, a drop, IK nonconvergence, or limit contact as failure and stop/replan rather than repeating nominal commands. A closed gripper is not grasp proof.\n\n**Handoff:** The validated open-skill exit is `drawer_position >= 0.29` at termination. The documented overlap with `red_transfer` covers actions 230:470: an earlier switch is represented once the drawer is above 0.26 m and red is exposed; the stronger nominal switch is after drawer motion is near zero, front contact is released, and closed fingers are accompanied by observable red/TCP upward co-motion. Success of the successor composition was not validated here."
  },
